From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: aperture: no decodebin3 between a raw-only camera and wrappercamerabinsrc

The camera source bin is pipewiresrc → capsfilter → decodebin3 → capsfilter (video/x-raw). decodebin3 answers caps
queries with the caps of its first stream, even after the stream moved to other caps. A full-resolution still (0105)
therefore failed on the first shot: 0105's capsfilter switched the camera to 2584x1944 (frames arrived), then
wrappercamerabinsrc's start_image_capture() cleared its src-capsfilter and asked upstream for the allowed caps, got
the 1152x864 viewfinder caps from decodebin3, intersected them with image-capture-caps 2584x1944 → EMPTY, and
pipewiresrc stopped with "not-negotiated" (GST_DEBUG on the SM-T550, snapshot r118).

A camera that offers only video/x-raw (every libcamera camera) needs no decoder, so the bin now links pipewiresrc →
capsfilter → capsfilter directly for such a camera. Cameras with compressed formats keep decodebin3. The bin is
built once, for the first camera Snapshot opens; a camera picked later that needs decoding would get no decoder
(not an issue on the SM-T550, whose cameras are both libcamera).

Without decodebin3, pipewiresrc's downstream caps query reached all of camerabin (converters, encoders) and took
4.7 s before the first frame (r119). The bin's last capsfilter now answers downstream caps queries itself with the
query's filter (as decodebin3 did, without asking downstream); camerabin converts any raw format, and its own
renegotiation queries travel upstream, which still passes through.
